Why: design 10 P4, "If it equals an outer open message instead, the inner ones are closed with truncated=True and
then it closes". The end marker of the outer 1000 (line 8) arrives while the inner 2154 is open: the 2154 is closed
truncated with its one body line, then the 1000 closes with a body of one line and the truncated 2154.

How: Written by hand (TLC did not produce this shape; research 1 tried). The messages around it are copied from tlc/v1.7.4/success.out: 2262 (version) and 2186 (finish). Lines 4 to 7 are lines 32, 33, 37 and 38 of
tlc/v1.7.4/java-override-exception.out (the 1000 start marker, its first line, the nested 2154 start marker and its
first line); the other lines of both messages and the 2154 end marker are left out, and line 8 is the 1000 end marker.
